tep 5: Compare the identified function with the given choices.**\nThe choices are:\nA) tonic\nB) subdominant\nC) dominant\nD) subtonic\n\nSince the Bb major chord is the diatonic chord built on the 7th degree (VII) of the C natural minor scale, its traditional functional name is the **subtonic**.\n\n**Conclusion:** The Bb chord functions as the subtonic in the key of C minor.\n\nAnswer: $\boxed{D}$
