roughout. (Incorrect. The first speaker shows surprise/concern.)\n*   D) first speaker shows surprise; second remains neutral. (This is identical to A, confirming the analysis.)\n\nSince both A and D state the same conclusion, and this conclusion accurately reflects the interaction (First speaker expresses surprise/concern; Second speaker remains neutral/procedural), I will select one of them.\n\nReasoning: The first speaker expresses surprise when asked for her birth certificate ("My my original birth certificate? But I don't carry that with me."). The second speaker maintains a neutral, procedural tone throughout the exchange ("Okay, let me see here," "Right. Well, we still need it.").\n\nAnswer: $\boxed{A}$
